  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef believes he can predict the weather just by looking at clouds!\n\nChef saw AAA clouds in the morning, and BBB clouds in the evening.\n\nHe believes that it will rain if the number of clouds he saw in the evening is **at least 333 times** of the number of the clouds he saw in the morning.\n\nGiven the values of AAA and BBB, what will Chef's prediction be?\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe only line of input contains two space-separated integers AAA and BBB — the number of clouds Chef saw in the morning and evening, respectively.\n\n\nOutput Format\nOutput a single line containing the answer: `Rain` if Chef believes it will rain, and `Dry` otherwise.\n\n\nEach character of the output may be printed in either uppercase or lowercase, i.e. the strings `dry`, `Dry`, `DrY`, and `dRY` are all considered equivalent.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤A,B≤201 \\leq A, B \\leq 201≤A,B≤20"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3 9",
        "output": "Rain",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nChef saw 333 clouds in the morning and 999 in the evening.\nSince 9≥3×39 \\geq 3\\times 39≥3×3, Chef believes it will rain."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4 9",
        "output": "Dry",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nChef saw 444 clouds in the morning and 999 in the evening.\nSince 9<3×4=129 \\lt 3\\times 4 = 129<3×4=12, Chef believes it will not rain."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "15 14",
        "output": "Dry",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nChef saw 151515 clouds in the morning and 141414 in the evening.\nSince 14<3×15=4514 \\lt 3\\times 15 = 4514<3×15=45, Chef believes it will not rain."
      }
    ]
  },
